On Tue, 7 Sep 2010, David Damerell wrote:
> Quoting  Patric Mueller  <bhaak@gmx.net>:
>> Elbereth doesn't work anymore on the major demons.
>> But for the early game it's still the same as Vanilla NetHack.
>> I'm still uncertain what to do with it.
>
> Well, if you want something a bit different to Spork, how about having it
> get used up - every time you use Elbereth, the chance of it working
> diminishes. It then becomes an emergency measure not a word to be stamped
> on every flat surface.

This is a good idea, because it takes care of the balance problem and thus 
indirectly of the interface problem as well. Also, I think it is nicely 
thematic: the more you use the word, the more monsters are aware that you 
are not really invincible.

One issue remains: powergamers will still be able to use the word very 
late.

David


